==English==
{{wikipedia|uncertainty principle}}
===Etymology===
named for [[w:Werner Heisenberg|Werner Heisenberg]], its discoverer

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|sg=[[w:Heisenberg|Heisenberg]] [[uncertainty]] [[principle]]}}

# {{quantum mechanics}} The principle that there is an [[absolute]] [[limit]] on the [[combined]] [[accuracy]] of certain [[pair]]s of [[simultaneous]], [[related]] [[measurement]]s, especially that of the [[position]] and [[momentum]] of a [[particle]].

====Synonyms====
* [[uncertainty principle]]
* [[indeterminacy principle]]

====Related terms====
* [[Planck's constant]]

